## Target Identity and Functional Architecture

S35-F3 preserves the S35-F2 identity: rounded red-mandarin peel, dry grapefruit pith, realistic pineapple flesh/skin relief, a restrained cassis shadow, moving Hedione-jasmone air, and a cedar-vetiver-Clearwood rear object projected by one clean outward musk. The only design change is the mineral-persistence stock.

The target function is not “more amber.” It is a continuous, dry, mineral rear plane that supports the fruit-to-wood transition without creating a warmer gourmand amber, an aggressive superamber spike, or a second musk effect. Ambrofix is selected because it is the owned ambergris-type material closest to that function. Ambrofix and Ambrox Super are distinct products; no sensory, strength, or performance equivalence is inferred.

